---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'

const updated = '2026-05-29'
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Tickbox"
  description="The terms for using Tickbox: the MIT-licensed OSS SDK and the paid cloud dashboard at app.tickbox.dev. Plain English, England & Wales."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[48rem] px-6 lg:px-10 py-20 lg:py-28">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">
        <strong>Legal</strong> · terms of service · last updated { updated }
      </p>
      <h1 class="display text-[clamp(2.5rem,5.5vw,4rem)] leading-[0.95] mb-6">
        Terms. <span class="italic-display text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Also the short version.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-lg text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-12 max-w-2xl">
        These terms cover using Tickbox — both the open-source SDK and the
        paid cloud dashboard. By installing the packages or signing in at
        app.tickbox.dev you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">1. Who we are</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Tickbox is operated by Tiny Systems Ltd, a company registered in
        England &amp; Wales ("we", "us"). Contact:
        <a href="mailto:hello@tinysystems.io" class="link-ink">hello@tinysystems.io</a>.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">2. The OSS SDK</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        The <code class="code-chip">@tickboxhq/*</code> packages are released
        under the MIT licence. You can use, modify and ship them in
        commercial products at no cost. The licence text in each package
        governs — including the "as is, no warranty" part. Nothing on this
        page restricts your rights under that licence.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">3. The cloud service</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-3">
        The dashboard at <code class="code-chip">app.tickbox.dev</code> and the
        ingest API at <code class="code-chip">api.tickbox.dev</code> are the
        paid (and free-tier) hosted service. To use them you create an
        account and keep your API keys confidential. You're responsible for
        activity under your account and for having a lawful basis to collect
        the consent records you send us.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        We aim for high availability but the service is provided without an
        uptime guarantee unless you have a separate written Enterprise
        agreement.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">4. Plans, billing &amp; cancellation</h2>
      <ul class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Every account starts on the <strong>Free</strong> tier — no card required.</li>
        <li>Paid plans (Entry £9, Pro £29, Unlimited £99 per month, in GBP) are billed monthly in advance through Stripe. Card data is handled by Stripe; we never see it.</li>
        <li>You can upgrade, downgrade or cancel anytime from the dashboard's billing page. Cancellation stops the next renewal; we don't refund the current period unless the law requires it.</li>
        <li>Plans carry usage limits (sites, monthly events, retention window). Exceed the event limit and ingest returns 429 until the next billing period or an upgrade.</li>
        <li>We may change prices with at least 30 days' notice to the account email; changes never apply to a period you've already paid for.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Prices shown exclude VAT where applicable; VAT is added at checkout
        based on your billing location.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Don't use the service to break the law, send data you have no right
        to send, attempt to deanonymise visitors, probe or overload our
        infrastructure, or resell the hosted service as your own. We can
        suspend an account that does — we'll tell you why.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        The audit log is designed to hold a salted/hashed visitor identifier,
        not raw personal data. Don't deliberately push direct identifiers
        (names, emails, raw IPs) into the event payload.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">6. Your data</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        How we handle data is in the
        <a href="/privacy" class="link-ink">Privacy Policy</a>. In short: the
        consent records you send remain yours; you can export them (CSV) or
        delete them (delete a site, or close the account) at any time. For
        the cloud service we act as your processor for those records; you're
        the controller.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">7. Liability</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Tickbox is a tool that helps you implement consent; it is not legal
        advice and using it doesn't by itself make you compliant. To the
        extent the law allows, our total liability for the service is capped
        at the fees you paid us in the 12 months before the claim, and we're
        not liable for indirect or consequential loss. Nothing here limits
        liability that can't be limited by law.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule-soft my-10" />

      <h2 class="display text-2xl mb-3">8. Changes &amp; governing law</h2>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-3">
        We may update these terms; material changes get a note in our release
        announcement and a new date at the top. Continuing to use the service
        after a change means you accept it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        These terms are governed by the laws of England &amp; Wales, and the
        courts of England &amp; Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <p class="eyebrow mt-12">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">← Back to tickbox.dev</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[color:var(--color-rule-soft)]">·</span>
        <a href="/privacy" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">Privacy</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .link-ink {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .link-ink:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }
</style>
